---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---
<Base>

<Hero crumbs={[{ href: "/services", label: "Services" }, { label: "Case studies" }]} kicker="Case studies" title="The same need for clarity." lede="Explore the kinds of questions Sterling helps business owners work through. These examples are representative and are not promises of results." />

<section class="wrap section grid3">
  <article class="panel">
    <p class="kicker">Professional practice</p>
    <h2>A specialist practice builds more retirement capacity</h2>
    <p>A high-earning practice explored a Cash Balance structure alongside its existing retirement plan to create more room for owner-directed savings.</p>
    <p>The question was not “what is the maximum.” It was whether the clinical staff who met the age and service rules had been priced before anyone quoted a partner credit. That is the same question on <a href="/physicians">physicians</a> and <a href="/staff-cost">staff cost</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel">
    <p class="kicker">Consulting business</p>
    <h2>An owner-led consultancy turns a scattered process into a calendar</h2>
    <p>With plan administration spread across multiple providers, the business needed a clearer operating rhythm and one partner to coordinate the details.</p>
    <p>The plan did not need a new slogan. It needed one census, one set of deadlines, and a named administrator. That operating rhythm is <a href="/administration">administration</a> and the <a href="/calendar">deadline calendar</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel">
    <p class="kicker">Established business</p>
    <h2>A mature business brings the next chapter into focus</h2>
    <p>A business owner used a structured planning conversation to connect current income, contribution capacity, and a more confident retirement timeline.</p>
    <p>Age changes the shape of a defined benefit credit. It does not create a private number you can copy from a colleague. The teaching contrast is on <a href="/illustrations">illustrations</a>, and it is not a quote.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="alt"><div class="wrap section max-prose">
  <h2>What these examples are not</h2>
  <p>They are not client results, deduction amounts, or a promise that your practice will look like the one in the paragraph. Sterling Pension Group does not publish a contribution as if it were an IRS limit. If a page shows a dollar figure that is not a statutory ceiling, it is illustrative and it depends on facts we state next to it. Change the census and the number changes.</p>
  <p>Your business has its own version of the story. The useful version starts with entity, compensation, and the people on payroll.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="wrap cta-section"><div class="cta">
  <div><h2>Your business has its own version of the story.</h2><p>Bring the facts. We will not retrofit a case study onto them.</p></div>
  <a class="btn gold" href="/contact">Start with your facts</a>
</div></section>

</Base>
